PTY-cycle diagnostic (pty-close-diagnostic.log), subprocess Python with
owned openpty master, setsid/TIOCSCTTY slave, raw 64MiB write, no master read.
After select observed output, SIGKILL exact owned PID; WNOHANG for 250ms.
8 running + 8 observed SIGSTOP trials: all remained ?Es, no waitable status
while master held. Closing master allowed all to reap -9 in <=6.14ms after
that 250ms window. Stopped arm additionally sent SIGCONT after master close.
The 8 non-stopped trials isolate the held-master mechanism from staging.
Diagnostic child exit=0. No primary keys, keychain or real transcripts used.

Implementation: NOTE_EXIT on the existing mio kqueue for exact owned PIDs;
EV_ADD ESRCH handles an already-exiting process. macOS can make that PID
unattachable before its waitpid status is ready, so reaping is nonblocking.
Only an already-notified exit retries in tick while its PTY drains; running
seats never poll child status. No global waitpid(-1), SIGCHLD ownership,
per-active-seat thread or second runtime. Non-macOS old polling fallback
is deliberately unchanged and UNVALIDATED.

Shutdown: flush coalesced capture, signal owned group/exact child, close the
single Option-owned PTY master, then event wait/nonblocking retry bounded at
250ms per child (not an overall 250ms actor-shutdown guarantee). A private
short-lived shutdown kqueue cannot consume other seats' runtime events.
An unconfirmed wait logs seat/generation/PID instead of blocking forever.
Confirmed shutdown exit is captured once after output. Normal runtime retains
its existing drain-before-Exit path. The owned profile driver now has a 360s
watchdog and reports actual exit, so a failed teardown cannot hide indefinitely.

